So hopefully the SOP layout is self-explanatory for the most part but just in case:\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li567\fi6\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95Each folder is for a course, within each course folder there\'92s usually folders for specific resources (quizzes, textbooks, etc.). \
\'95Files within the folders usually have the year and number (if applicable). For example, assignment 3 for a course from 2019 would be in the assignments folder for the course with the name \'912019-3\'92. \
\'95Textbooks are named after their author. If two files would\'92ve had similar names, e.g., both were notes on the course, and they were in the same folder, numbering of files starts at 0 (e.g., there\'92s a \'91notes0\'92, \'91notes1\'92, etc.) \
\'95If files had an unknown date, a \'91?\'92 was used.\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Of course there\'92s exceptions to these conventions but have a look around and see if you can find anything useful!\
